 "description": "Male Sydney funnel-web spider (Atrax robustus) in its rearing threat pose, facing right: glossy blue-black body (#2a2f38, not pure black) with blue-grey shine highlights so it reads on dark backgrounds, bare shiny carapace tilted up, front legs raised high, eight thick legs (far-side legs a shade lighter), mating spur on the second leg, finger-like spinnerets, big chelicerae with two large downward-pointing fangs (no drops). Anchor bottom-centre (feet on y=0); bbox x -232..+230, y -305..0; fangs (two, ~55 long) hang from (+150..+172,-222) to y -168, chelicerae at (+150,-240).",
